{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== CORRECTION TO THE PRECEDING COMMENT: \"J11 IS COMPLETE\" IS WRONG. ===\n\nThe preceding comment's headline said \"J11 IS COMPLETE\". It is not, and I am correcting it here\nrather than leaving a false claim in the trail. What is true and what is not:\n\nTRUE, and unchanged: the run is 26/26 green, and the EPIC'S HEADLINE AC is proven live in both\ndirections — a DC-created issue reaches the local store, and a local edit reaches the DC issue. The\nevidence and the oracle analysis in the two preceding comments stand.\n\nFALSE: that this STORY's acceptance criteria are met. A close attempt returned FIVE unmet criteria,\nand on inspection every one of them is a genuine gap, not a documentation gap:\n\n 1. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py` DOES NOT EXIST. This ticket's own\n    `file_impact` names it and the plan-review signature already recorded `dep absent\n    tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py`. Only the THIN VERTICAL SLICE is implemented —\n    one inbound create and one outbound title edit. Of the plan's 28-cell table (14 inbound x 14\n    outbound), 26 cells are unwritten.\n 2. Per-mutation IDEMPOTENCE after each direction is not asserted. The existing\n    `test_a_repeated_dc_reconcile_pass_writes_nothing` runs against an EMPTY `dc_rebar_repo`, not\n    against the real store copy and not per mutation.\n 3. PAGINATION is not exercised at all: nothing observes the effective server page size, seeds\n    2*observed+1 issues, or asserts full recovery.\n 4. The inbound assignee path does not POSITIVELY assert an identity was minted (that the returned\n    id is the ticket's assignee and the provider is the `jira` family). The transport-level\n    `test_name_identity_user_search_resolves_a_real_user_authoritatively` is a different assertion.\n 5. The \"this project's live Jira is untouched\" AC requires a FILE-CONTENT check collecting every\n    `base_url` assignment in the working repo and asserting the distinct set is exactly the harness\n    URL. No such test exists.\n\nWHY I GOT THIS WRONG, since it is worth recording: I read the harness going green as the story going\ngreen. It is not the same claim. The thin slice was designed to prove the RISKIEST criterion first —\nthat data moves in both directions — and it did exactly that. But \"the riskiest AC is satisfied\" is\nnot \"all ACs are satisfied\", and the close gate was right to hold the line. This is the same\ndistinction handoff #4 drew when it warned that a converged pass over an empty store is not evidence\nof function; the failure mode here is the mirror image — a real, meaningful green being over-read.\n\nSTATUS: this story stays IN PROGRESS. The remaining work is the comprehensive mutation suite and the\nfour other criteria above, all of which are live-harness test authoring against the existing fixtures\n(`bound_dc_issue`, `dc_store_copy_repo`, `dc_transport`, `_seed_searchable_issue`,\n`_wait_until_searchable`) rather than production-code change."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785620073049740001,"uuid":"de206465-7645-490a-a262-febeb5967ec4"}